<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 6th Grade (CEFR: A2.1)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Community News</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Our Community Is Famous For...</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: text_1: Write simple interpretations of common texts in English supported with visual aids. text_2: Explain the main points of class readings to peers.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can write simple summaries of community news articles with visual support (e.g., uses an image of the parade as an aid for the summary, 'The Desfile de las Mil Polleras took place last weekend. Many women wore colorful polleras and danced in the streets.'). Can explain the main points of class readings about Panamanian traditions using visuals (e.g., shows pictures of Carnival floats and attendees while explaining, 'The text talks about Carnival in Chitré. People enjoy the parades and music.'). Can simplify event flyers for peers, highlighting key details with visuals (e.g., 'The school fair is on Friday at 9 a.m.' with a drawing of a calendar and school, or 'The Fiestas Patrias parade starts at 10 a.m.' with a picture of a marching band).</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; text-align: left;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; text-align: left;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; text-align: left;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a collage of pictures showcasing various Panamanian community traditions previously discussed (e.g., Desfile de las Mil Polleras, Chitré Carnival, artisan market). Students identify the events and recall key vocabulary. Teacher asks: "What do you remember about the Desfile de las Mil Polleras? Who participated?" or "What did people do during Carnival?" This activates past tense recall and descriptive adjectives.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to simply explain an event from one of the pictures using past simple and descriptive adjectives. For example, pointing to a picture of an artisan, the teacher says: "Last weekend, I visited the artisan market. I saw a friendly artisan. He was tall and wore a sombrero pintao. He sold many colorful crafts." Teacher explicitly demonstrates pronunciation of past tense -ed endings (e.g., 'visited' /ɪd/, 'saw' - irregular, 'wore' - irregular, 'sold' - irregular) and short/long vowel sounds (e.g., /æ/ in 'crafts' vs. /eɪ/ in 'display').</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I describe the artisan, am I talking about him now or in the past?" (Expected answer: "In the past.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do I use many difficult words or easy words to explain this picture?" (Expected answer: "Easy words.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Our Community News".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher presents two short, simplified "community news" texts or event flyers from a local fictional newsletter, each accompanied by a relevant visual aid (e.g., image of a parade, a community fair banner, a drawing of a market). One text describes a past event (e.g., "The School Fair was a success!"), and the other is a simplified flyer for an upcoming cultural event (e.g., "Community Festival Next Saturday!"). The texts incorporate past simple, descriptive adjectives, and relevant vocabulary (e.g., community, fair, parade, festival, artisan, prepare, celebrate, colorful).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Mediation: Explain the main points of class readings to peers.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students read the texts silently. Then, the teacher asks simple gist questions:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is Text 1 about?" (e.g., "A school fair.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When was the school fair?" (e.g., "Last weekend.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is Text 2 about?" (e.g., "A community festival.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When is the community festival?" (e.g., "Next Saturday.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Mediation.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice writing simple interpretations/summaries, explaining main points, and simplifying texts. Focus on past simple tense, compound sentences with 'but', descriptive adjectives for people and events, and relevant vocabulary (reporter, news, parade, festival, decorate, participate, proud, excited).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Summary Matching):</b> The teacher provides sentence beginnings from the news texts/flyers and students complete them with relevant information, or match a simple sentence to a corresponding picture/detail. For instance, "The festival was _______." (colorful / excited). Or students fill in gaps: "Many people ______ (celebrate) the parade. The Carnival Queen ______ (wear) a beautiful dress." Teacher guides pronunciation of -ed endings.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Group Summarization with Visuals):</b> In small groups, students receive a short, different text (e.g., about a historical community event like Fiestas Patrias, or a local talent show) with a picture. They work together to write a 2-3 sentence summary of the text, focusing on the main points and using past simple and descriptive adjectives. Each group must also create a simple drawing or sketch as a visual aid for their summary. Example sentence frame: "The text was about _______. People ______ (verb) and ______ (verb). I liked ______, but I didn't like ______." (This reinforces compound sentences and softening disagreement).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction (Peer Explanation):</b> Each group exchanges their summary and visual aid with another group. Students take turns acting as a "junior reporter" to explain their group's summary and visual aid to their partner, simplifying the information if needed. Partners ask clarifying questions. They practice sharing past experiences and preferences, and softening disagreement (e.g., "I understood the main idea, but maybe you can explain more about 'who' participated?").</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-17 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Our Community News".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format: Community Traditions Mural Explanation.</b> Students, individually or in their project groups (if applicable), will present their "Community Traditions Mural" project to the class. They will act as a "community reporter" sharing important news about their community's traditions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each student/group stands next to their mural (or a drawing/photo of their mural).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They will explain the tradition depicted on their mural to the class, using the mural as a visual aid.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They must use the past simple tense to describe the event or tradition (e.g., "The Desfile de las Mil Polleras took place last weekend. Many women wore colorful polleras and danced in the streets.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They must incorporate descriptive adjectives (e.g., "The artisan wore a sombrero pintao. He was tall and friendly.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They can express preferences using 'but' (e.g., "I liked the music, but I didn't like the crowd.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They are encouraged to simplify the information for their peers, explaining any challenging concepts.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">After each presentation, other students can ask questions. The presenter mediates answers, ensuring clarity.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy and student self-reflection.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students present their "Community Traditions Mural" explanation (as described in Stage 4) to the class. The teacher observes and assesses their ability to mediate information.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Observation Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of explanation and main points.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of past simple tense.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of descriptive adjectives.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effective use of visual aid (mural/drawing).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation (especially -ed endings).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate vocabulary from the unit.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete the following prompts:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can explain the main ideas of my community's tradition using English. Yes / No"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I used a picture/drawing to help explain my tradition. Yes / No"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one thing you learned about explaining community traditions in English today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of your mural explanation was easy, and what was challenging?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What aspects of the mediation tasks worked well? Did students effectively simplify information and use visual aids?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for students to better explain and summarize texts for their peers? (e.g., more sentence starters, explicit modeling of simplifying complex vocabulary).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How did the "Community Traditions Mural" project help integrate the language skills learned throughout the unit?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> This lesson concludes the theme "Our Community Is Famous For..." and the "Community Traditions Mural" project. The next lesson will begin a new theme, possibly reviewing key vocabulary and grammar in a different context.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>